<title>USA: Matrix Capital Corp FY 96 net decreased.</title>
<headline>Matrix Capital Corp FY 96 net decreased.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands,</p>
<p>						   except per share data)</p>
<p>							    Year Ended</p>
<p>						   Dec 31	    Dec 31</p>
<p>						     1996		1995</p>
<p> Total interest income		  16,492	    10,730</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses		    143		 401</p>
<p>  Gain on sale of loans		     3,369	     3,272</p>
<p>  Gain on sale of servicing		 3,232	     1,164</p>
<p> Net income				 3,273	     3,561</p>
<p>Net income excluding FDIC special</p>
<p>   assessment				   3,541	     3,561</p>
<p> FDIC special assessment, net of taxes    268		  --</p>
<p>     Net income				 3,273	     3,561</p>
<p> Net income per share			 $     0.76 $     0.91</p>
<p>Weighted average common and common</p>
<p>   equiv. shares outstanding		 4,297,448  3,927,629</p>
<p>Shares outstanding at the end</p>
<p>   of the period				 5,901,439  3,888,939</p>
<p>(1) Non-performing loans and non-performing assets include $738,000 of non-accrual, sub-prime auto loans repurchased by Sterling Finance Co Inc subject to limited recourse provisions of loan sale agreements.</p>
<p>The allowance for loan losses does not include a $600,000 liability reserve account to cover potential losses associated with the loans repurchased by Sterling Finance Co Inc subject to limited recourse provisions of loan sale agreements.</p>
<p>The increase in the number of shares was due to a stock offering completed in October 1996.</p>
</text>
